      "updated": 1785349994205,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's understand by taking example of n = 18; \n\nfactors of n - \n            \n                    1 x 18 = 18\n                    2 x 9 = 18\n                    3 x 6 = 18\n                    \n                    after > root of 18 - 4.5 pairs starts repeating \n\n                    6 x 3 = 18\n                    9 x 2 = 18\n                    18 x 1 = 18\n                    ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's understand by taking example of n = 18; \n\nfactors of n - \n            \n                    1 x 18 = 18\n                    2 x 9 = 18\n                    3 x 6 = 18\n                    \n                    after > root of 18 - 4.5 pairs starts repeating \n\n                    6 x 3 = 18\n                    9 x 2 = 18\n                    18 x 1 = 18\n                    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
